{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## WITHDRAWN — the central claim is false, and I disproved it myself\n\nThis ticket asserts the close gate's `provenance:` requirement and plan-review's 8,000-character\nadmission cap are \"mutually unsatisfiable\". **They are not.** Measured on the exact ticket I filed\nthis from:\n\n```\nORIGINAL description : 7989 chars — 14 acceptance criteria, 105 lines of narrative prose\nLEAN rewrite         : 4440 chars — ALL 14 criteria + ALL 9 provenance lines\nheadroom under cap   : 3560 chars (44% spare)\n```\n\nThe complete, fully gate-compliant description fits in **4,440 characters**. I produced that\nrewrite myself, as the \"workaround\", and then filed a bug claiming the thing I had just done was\nimpossible.\n\n### What actually happened\n\n`darkish-enormous-raptors` carried **105 lines of narrative prose** for a cleanup task — method\ndiscussion, rationale, and context that belonged in comments. That is roughly 3,500 characters of\nmaterial a plan does not need to state, and it is what consumed the budget. The provenance lines\nwere the last straw on an already-overweight description, not the cause.\n\n**8,000 characters is ample for one ticket's worth of work.** It is around 1,200 words. A plan that\ncannot state its problem and its acceptance criteria in that space is describing more than one unit\nof work, or is padding. Mine was padding.\n\n### The cap did its job\n\nA budget that refuses an over-described plan is working. I experienced the refusal as an\nobstruction and reframed my own verbosity as a system defect — including inventing a false\ngenerality (\"above a certain number of external criteria no ordering satisfies both\") that the\n44% headroom flatly contradicts.\n\nThe four review cycles were caused by **my successive description edits**, not by any gate\ninteraction. Each edit staled the attestation exactly as designed.\n\n### Nothing survives worth keeping open\n\n- The claimed incompatibility: **disproven by measurement.**\n- \"Provenance lines are gate-mandated boilerplate that shouldn't count\": unnecessary — they fit\n  comfortably when the description is proportionate.\n- Discoverability of the cap: an author learns it on first rejection, which is how most limits are\n  learned, and the message is clear. Not worth a bug on this evidence.\n- The parallel to `bediasite-bilineate-stoat`: **misdrawn.** There, two gates genuinely demanded\n  mutually exclusive things. Here they demanded a shorter description, and a shorter description\n  existed.\n\nClosing `not_a_bug`. If someone later finds a ticket whose ACs ALONE exceed the cap, that is a\ndifferent and real finding — file it with that evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787287931728003001,"uuid":"847ab08d-6851-4f25-b566-9d24efead0f9"}